# Files that must never be uploaded to Vercel.
#
# The Vercel CLI does NOT read .gitignore when it uploads a deployment - only its
# own built-in list plus this file - so anything kept out of git must be listed
# here too, or a manual `vercel` deploy ships it anyway.
#
# Local environment files. These MUST NOT ship.
#
# 9 Oct 2026: two backend builds deployed as Environment=Production were reading
# the PREVIEW database. The Vercel dashboard variables were right; the uploaded
# .env won. dotenv loads the file that travels with the bundle, so whatever
# DATABASE_URL sits in it overrides the dashboard, and the Environment label on
# a deployment stops meaning anything about which database it talks to. QA spent
# about an hour on the wrong data, and admin@gmail.com — a super_admin in
# production, a caregiver in preview — could not log in.
#
# `vercel env pull` is what puts a file like .env.vercel here, so this has to
# hold whatever name it lands under.
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Generated reports, guides, walkthroughs, invoices, proposals and proof screenshots.
# Root-anchored on purpose: the backend deploys from the committed dist/, so an
# unanchored rule must never be added here.
/*.html
/*.pdf
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.docx
/*.xlsx
/*.csv
qa-shots/
qa-evidence/
qa-regression/
figma-refs/
